  "id": "consolidation-period",
  "term": "consolidation period",
  "definition": "In distraction osteogenesis, the consolidation period is the phase after bone separation in which the newly formed tissue hardens and becomes stronger bone. A long consolidation period means this strengthening stage takes a relatively long time and can limit the overall procedure.",
